# @hub-lanes
# PR-pair canary (BH-632): two OPEN PRs failing the same job with the same first
# error means main is probably red, hours before main's own run history says so.
# WRITES: the main_red_pairs rows (one open row per condition), the
# main_red_pr_errors rows (one terminal verdict per head sha) and
# logs/main-red-pr-pair.log (BH-4156). With no row store (no JOBS_URL or
# HARNESS_SECRET, or a worker without the routes) the files are the record:
# state/main-red/pairs/ and state/main-red/pr-errors/.
# WRITES NO flags/main-red-* EXCEPT the suspected freeze (BH-1451): when a pair
# fires AND the detector's verdict (the main_red_verdicts row, or
# state/main-red/<slug>.verdict with no row store) has no decision, this
# lane raises flags/main-red-<slug> (owner=main-red-pr-pair) and clears it on the
# first complete look with no pair. Where the detector HAS decided — red, green,
# or no verdict at all — the freeze stays its business, because a pair can
# be one shared flake.
*/10 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/main-red-pr-pair.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
